{"type":"transaction","version":1,"events":[{"type":"new_task","ts":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.793768Z","data":{"id":"QPVZIC","uuid":"e348cb89-42f3-4524-b6b7-e8dc7a97e44b","epic_id":"","state":"todo","title":"Oracle migration skill and MB01UD pilot","body":"","created_at":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.793768Z"}},{"type":"new_task","ts":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.794354Z","data":{"id":"I62JLM","uuid":"396d63de-cc25-40fa-8d63-acf7683f4a73","epic_id":"QPVZIC","state":"draft","title":"Build the MB01UD reference oracle and contract","body":"## Goal\nEstablish an independent executable reference for a bounded Hessenberg product migration.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nCompile pinned MB01UD against OpenBLAS, record compiler/backend/source identity, and document row/column-major conversion, valid domain, ignored storage, errors, and API differences.\n## Validation Gates\nRun a hand-checkable asymmetric case through the Fortran executable and confirm the input buffers are restored.","created_at":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.794354Z"}},{"type":"new_task","ts":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.794358Z","data":{"id":"GIPOSC","uuid":"47803127-2a33-474b-ae39-cf6a56e34639","epic_id":"QPVZIC","state":"draft","title":"Translate MB01UD and build differential acceptance","body":"## Goal\nImplement the Hessenberg product with Gonum BLAS and a replayable side-by-side oracle runner.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nCover side/transpose combinations, zero/scalar/rectangular/padded matrices, finite scale extremes, invalid arguments, untouched inputs, and output padding. Comparator rejects nonfinite mismatches, status mismatches, missing output, and deliberate mutations.\n## Validation Gates\nRun the deterministic oracle corpus, replay saved JSON cases, and run persistent Go and harness checks.","created_at":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.794358Z"}},{"type":"new_task","ts":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.794361Z","data":{"id":"VW6UP2","uuid":"fb77d3bc-9d14-416b-9bd4-0777d08b9432","epic_id":"QPVZIC","state":"draft","title":"Create and refine the oracle migration skill and playbook","body":"## Goal\nDeliver a reusable repository-local skill and practical playbook grounded in the completed pilot.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nInclude discovery, an executable reference, contract mapping, numerical comparisons, mismatch triage, acceptance gates, and a repeatable refinement loop. Record demonstrated limitations and actual results.\n## Validation Gates\nValidate skill metadata and links, follow its acceptance procedure from a fresh build, and document observed refinements with evidence.","created_at":"2026-09-10T22:43:38.794361Z"}}]}
